{
 "description": "DEP-06 \u00a7Judging a proof: the history a fraud proof rests on, and what a member does when its replica lacks it. `needs` is FraudProof::history_needs / fr:proof-history-needs: the (ledger_id, sequence) pairs a verifier's replica must have reached before a failed verification means the proof is invalid. A fault update at seq N follows one at N-1 at the latest; an omission rests on the accused's update at its proof sequence (proof_sequence, or the proof_update's own sequence); QuorumExpired and WinnerCollateralDeviation rest on none. Needs are at the proof level: a type that requires an embedding (UncreditedLightningPayment) adds the embedding's update, and cl declines such types. `verdicts`: `tips` maps a ledger to our replica's tip sequence (null: no replica held), `verifies` is the verification result; `expect` is `judge` (it verified: act on it), `park` (it failed and a need is unmet: hold it, catch up, judge it again; MUST NOT be treated as invalid), or `refuse` (it failed with every need met: invalid). From regtest run 1120-075609 (2026-11-20T08:02:51Z): ref7, 3 s behind 7341c3d1 at seq 4, refused four seq-9 NonConformingUpdate proofs for good. Generated; shared by deposits-rust (deposits-protocol/tests/vectors), cl-deposits (inspect/vectors) and the spec (vectors/).",
